  "term": "impression",
  "definition": "In historical psychology and philosophy, an impression can mean a direct perceptual experience, contrasted with an idea as a fainter revived form of that experience. It can also mean the bodily stimulation process considered apart from the sensation it produces, and in some sociological usage it was used to mean constraint.",
